# Private repository safety

- Treat this workspace as **confidential enterprise source**.
- Never instruct the user to paste secrets, `.env`, private keys, or customer data into public chats.
- Prefer reading only files needed for the current task.
- If a path matches deny patterns (`.env`, `*.pem`, credentials), refuse to open/export it and explain why.
- Do not run destructive git commands (`push --force`, hard reset to shared branches) unless the user explicitly asks.
- When unsure whether a file is safe for context, ask before reading.
